          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "गुसलख़ाना — gusalkhānā — \"a bathroom\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "हमारे कमरे का गुसलख़ाना छोटा है। hamāre kamre kā gusalkhānā choṭā hai. The bathroom in our room is small."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "गुसलख़ाना (gusalkhānā) is usually traced to Persian ġusl-khāna, a room (khāna) for washing (ġusl); Hindi speech smooths ġusl to gusal."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
